Combination Table
To open the Combination Table, click this button.
Remarks
Type the Trigger objects which Plant Simulation combines into the combination trigger into the cells of the
table.
• Type the name of a TimeSequence into the column Time Sequence. You can access the TimeSequence
in the connection Formula with this name. Click one of the entries to open the respective value list.
• Type the path to the source Trigger into the column Origin.
• Type when the Trigger starts working into the column Start Time.
• Type how often the Trigger is going to repeat into the column Count.
• Type when the Trigger stops working, independently of repeated patterns, into the column End Time. If
you do not specify a value, no end time applies.
SimTalk
CombinationTable [SimTalk]
compute [SimTalk]
Combination Table
11-4348 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Formula [Trigger]
For the Combination Trigger you can type in a formula that computes the Trigger’s value pattern.
Remarks
The formula connects the Trigger objects, which you typed into the Combination Table. The allowed
operations depend on the data type of the involved Triggers.
• For a TimeSequence of data type boolean, you can use the boolean operators AND, OR, and NOT.
• For a TimeSequence with numerical data types, you can use the operators +, -, *, and /.
Example
TRIGGER AND TRIGGER2 AND TRIGGER3
weeklyPlan AND dailyPlan
employeenum - 2
SimTalk
Formula [SimTalk]
